design:
Module requirements should include `baseSystemId`, compatible base versions, required packs, and optional packs. For the first implementation, exact base system and required pack presence are enough; version ranges can be represented as strings and interpreted conservatively. Use provider-neutral `rulesRef` in fixtures and DB JSON.

Initial test sketch:
```ts
const pack = validateModulePack({ ...module, meta: { ...module.meta, rulesRequirements: dndRequirements } });
expect(pack.encounters[0].creatures[0].rulesRef).toBe('creature:goblin');
expect(() => createCampaign(db, { campaignId: 'c1', pack: EMBERFALL_HOLLOW, rulesBinding: pathfinderBinding })).toThrow(CampaignError);
```
